{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103599","id":2371964045,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6NYUyN","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103599","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103599.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103599.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103599","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103599/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103599/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103599/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0dbd8c076cf9ef3904021f6060e9c594c7de219c","number":103599,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Implement a conversion plugin to bake noise textures","user":{"login":"cfare","id":9624747,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MjQ3NDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9624747?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare","html_url":"https://github.com/cfare","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfare/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Overview\r\nImplements a conversion plugin that allows NoiseTexture2D resources to be converted to WebP or PNG files and reimported as CompressedTexture2D.\r\n\r\nThe motivating use case for this is using a high-resolution noise texture that does not need to be altered after being initially configured - e.g. driving a wave effect in a shader. NoiseTexture2Ds are regenerated when the scene is loaded, and can take many seconds at high resolutions, which can be really annoying when trying to iterate quickly during development, or adversely impact load times in finished projects.\r\n\r\nIn my own use cases I rarely need to modify a noise texture after setting it up, and if that is required it's still simple enough to recreate it. I assume this is true of many users.\r\n\r\nThis is my first PR so please excuse me if I missed something obvious!\r\n\r\n### Implementation\r\nThe existing conversion plugin design does not allow interactivity - conversions are performed immediately and cannot prompt the user for input. This PR also adds the necessary plumbing for asynchronous conversions. Plugins can optionally implement the `convert_async` function which calls a callback when the conversion is complete.\r\n\r\nThe new `NoiseTextureConversionPlugin` implements this. It opens a dialog to allow the user to select the save location of the new file.\r\n\r\n### Alternative implementations\r\nI considered 3 possible implementations of async conversions:\r\n* Add a new `EditorResourceAsyncConversionPlugin` in addition to the existing `EditorResourceConversionPlugin`. Because the interface is different it would require doubling up all the places conversion plugins are currently plumbed in (the filesystem dock, the resource picker, the `find_resource_conversion_plugin` functions etc) with an async version of each.\r\n* Modify the existing `EditorResourceConversionPlugin` to always support asynchronous conversions. `EditorResourceConversionPlugin::convert` would always take a callback, and the existing non-async plugins could just call it immediately.\r\n* Add `convert_async` to the existing `EditorResourceConversionPlugin`, which may return null when the plugin doesn't support async conversions. Likewise, plugins could return null for `convert` if they don't support normal conversions. This way users can try an async conversion if a normal conversion fails.\r\n\r\nI opted for the third option because it involved the smallest change to existing code. Option one would involve a lot of almost-duplicate code which didn't seem very elegant. Option two is probably the cleanest but would be an API break and involve changing all existing conversion plugins - I'm a first-time contributor so I don't know what the appetite is for this kind of change\r\n\r\nI am more than happy to try one of the other proposed implementations (or indeed anything else) if that would be more desirable.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_